//? Title: Stooge sort: actual overlapping recursive calls
//? Subtitle: Actual canonical histories, retained original fixtures and explicit controls
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Stooge sort compares endpoints, then sorts overlapping two-thirds ranges three
times. Its deliberately expensive recursion makes the difference between
asymptotic references and actual executed calls visible.
)

\toc

> Mechanism and mathematical scope

For length n>2 recurse on the first n-floor(n/3), last n-floor(n/3), then first
range again. Each invocation makes one endpoint comparison. Thus
C(n)=1+3*C(ceil(2n/3)) for n>2, with C(2)=1. Rounding creates plateaus;
n^log_(3/2)(3), approximately n^2.71, is an asymptotic reference rather than the
exact count. This implementation records completed calls in postorder, with any
endpoint exchange occurring before its children.

> A tiny actual producing history

The table and native concept diagram read the same producing execution. Every
block below is a complete editable C++ program.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/stooge_sort_tiny.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <print>
#include <algorithm>
#include <cmath>
#include <limits>
#include <numeric>
#include <numbers>
#include <random>
#include <string>
#include <vector>
#include <map>
#include <set>
#include <array>
#include <tuple>
#include <bit>
#include <datamunge/random/quality.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/stooge_sort.hpp>
int main() {
    namespace a = dm::algorithms;
    namespace g = dm::graphics;
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    auto r = a::stooge_sort_trace(std::vector<int>{3, 1, 2});
    std::print("| actual range | depth | endpoint swapped | complete actual post-call keys |\n| --- | ---: " "| --- | --- |\n");
    for (const auto &s : r.steps)
        std::print("| {}..{} | {} | {} | `{}` |\n", s.first, s.last, s.depth,
                   s.swapped, s.after);
    g::Diagram concept_diagram(48, 1100);
    concept_diagram.node("n0", {0, 0}, "Actual input3,1,2");
    concept_diagram.node("n1", {5, 0},
                         std::format("{} actual endpoint comparisons",
                                     r.comparisons));
    concept_diagram.node("n2", {10, 0},
                         std::format("Actual sorted {}", r.values));
    concept_diagram.edge("n0", "n1").edge("n1", "n2");
    concept_diagram.save_svg("build/stooge_sort_tiny.svg");
}
```
