> API and interpretation

Generic copyable keys require a strict weak ordering. Floating nonfinite keys
fail. The compatibility in-place sort replaces caller data only after successful
completion of the owned run. Default work limits protect against explosive
execution. Endpoint exchanges are unstable; no stability claim is made. The
original count-only report recurrence is replaced with actual executions for
every n through200.

Reusable producers, fixtures and histories live in the canonical C++ library.
Captured records own their values and do not come from a separate report replay.
Selected counters and record/scalar policies are specified at their API
boundaries; they are not peak-byte or wall-time budgets. Synthetic structural
inputs are controlled fixtures for these mechanisms.

> References

- Cormen et al., Introduction to Algorithms, stooge-sort recurrence exercise

Verified in the shared ten-document batch: 58 scoped native cases;20 directly
instrumented ASan/UBSan cases;90 executable public examples;416/416 definitions
across25 full scopes;10 hovers;1968 independent records/417332 checks;frozen
comparisons across all ten families with SIP returned-iterate correction
recorded;14 checkout/installed standalone headers and linked ten-family
consumer;40 executed programs and40 inspected figures with both exports.
Receipts: `build/mepml-conversion/batch-374-383/`.
